  words:
  - siphonaptera
  - siphonapteras
  - flea
  - fleas
  info: "The order siphonaptera, better known as fleas, are small insects that live
    as external parasites of mammals and birds. Adults are typically about an eighth
    of an inch long, allowing them to move easily through their hosts\u2019 fur or
    feathers. They are excellent jumpers, with some species able to leap up to 50
    times their body length. Their mouthparts are specialized for piercing skin and
    sucking blood from their hosts.\n\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flea "
  image: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 67f78deaa064ce54d825c7a33a812719, type: 3}
